1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,592
This video shows you how to build your first pipeline.

2
00:00:05,592 --> 00:00:10,950
It reads records from one Kafka topic, changes them, and sends them to another.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,393
You need two topics: one for the records coming in, and one for the result.

4
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:24,386
Send three records to the input topic, so there's something to capture.

5
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,035
In smeltr, open Build, and add a route.

6
00:00:29,035 --> 00:00:34,578
It takes records from a source, through a pipeline, to destinations.

7
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:40,838
Start with a new source.

8
00:00:40,838 --> 00:00:44,286
Pull, all workers, then Kafka.

9
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:47,961
Call it tutorial-in.

10
00:00:47,961 --> 00:00:52,723
Give it the broker, and the input topic, and add it.

11
00:00:56,520 --> 00:01:01,596
Main changes only when you deploy, so smeltr asks for a branch.

12
00:01:01,596 --> 00:01:04,350
Call it tutorial-first-pipeline.

13
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,110
Everything you save from here on goes on that branch.

14
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:09,790
Now make a new pipeline.

15
00:01:09,790 --> 00:01:11,284
It asks for a capture.

16
00:01:11,284 --> 00:01:14,951
A worker opens the source itself, reads a few records,

17
00:01:14,951 --> 00:01:18,430
and hands them back, without deploying anything.

18
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:23,391
Start at the earliest record, so the capture finds the three you sent.

19
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:30,241
There they are.

20
00:01:30,241 --> 00:01:33,829
Stop the capture, and use these records.

21
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:40,000
smeltr reads them, and proposes a first step.

22
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,817
It reads each record as JSON.

23
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,261
Add an Eval step.

24
00:01:45,261 --> 00:01:49,230
It sets fields to the values of expressions.

25
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,403
Make the message uppercase.

26
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:02,190
Then add a field that labels these records.

27
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:06,137
The dot puts dataset inside an event object.

28
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,855
Save the pipeline.

29
00:02:09,855 --> 00:02:12,087
You're back on the route.

30
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,101
Last, the destination.

31
00:02:15,101 --> 00:02:20,924
A new Kafka destination, tutorial-out, writes to the output topic.

32
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:37,179
The route reads tutorial-in, through tutorial-in-parse, to tutorial-out.

33
00:02:37,179 --> 00:02:38,434
Save it.

34
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:43,344
Before anything runs, check where the records go.

35
00:02:43,344 --> 00:02:45,958
Route the records you captured.

36
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,119
All three reach tutorial-out, changed the way you wanted.

37
00:02:51,119 --> 00:02:52,947
Nothing was sent.

38
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:56,569
It's all on your branch, and not deployed yet.

39
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,892
Check on learning.

40
00:03:02,092 --> 00:03:05,497
You saved a source, a pipeline and a destination.

41
00:03:05,497 --> 00:03:08,599
Why don't your workers run them yet?

42
00:03:12,999 --> 00:03:14,452
They're on a branch.

43
00:03:14,452 --> 00:03:19,121
Workers run main, and main changes only when you deploy.

44
00:03:20,021 --> 00:03:24,151
How did the capture read records, with nothing deployed?

45
00:03:28,551 --> 00:03:32,440
A worker opened the source itself and handed the records back.

46
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:38,057
It marks nothing as read, so your pipeline still gets every record when it runs.

47
00:03:38,957 --> 00:03:42,693
Next, you review this change and deploy it.
